  <name>Nordstjernen</name>
  <summary>A small, hand-written web browser</summary>
  <developer id="org.nordstjernen">
    <name>Andreas Røsdal</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Nordstjernen is a clean-room web browser written from scratch in C,
      with a GTK 4 user interface and a libcurl network stack. It is built
      to be small, secure, and readable by a single person end to end.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A from-scratch HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript engine — no forked browser engine.</li>
      <li>Each tab's engine runs in its own sandboxed process (seccomp + Landlock on Linux) behind an IPC and shared-memory framebuffer boundary.</li>
      <li>No JIT, which keeps the JavaScript attack surface small.</li>
      <li>Opt-in WebGL, gated by a per-site trust prompt.</li>
      <li>No telemetry: it does not phone home and does not track the user.</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

